Disable data reporting at compile time -- DESKTOP half (LW-M1-02).

Split out of upstream's patches/disable-data-reporting-at-compile-time.patch.
The hunks below are the ones that only exist in a desktop build, or only in the
desktop Firefox version (firefox-157.0; Android builds firefox-153.0esr, see
version.android). Everything else in the upstream patch is in
patches/disable-data-reporting-common.patch; common + desktop together are
byte-for-byte upstream's current patch.

  browser/moz.configure
      MOZ_SERVICES_HEALTHREPORT and MOZ_NORMANDY -> False. These are the two
      front-end inputs to MOZ_DATA_REPORTING (toolkit/moz.configure:3493-3507);
      turning them off is what takes the datareporting.policy.* block in
      modules/libpref/init/all.js out of the build.
      This file only exists for the desktop front end -- browser/app.mozbuild:11
      pulls /browser in and mobile/android/app.mozbuild never does -- so it can
      do nothing for Android. mobile/android/moz.configure:131-132 supplies the
      same two options with MOZ_SERVICES_HEALTHREPORT *True*; the Android
      equivalent of this hunk is
      patches/android/disable-data-reporting-android.patch.

  python/sites/mach.txt
      Comments out the glean-sdk pypi requirement. The pinned version is part of
      the context (68.0.1 on 157), so the hunk is version-specific; the 153esr
      variant (67.3.2) is in patches/android/disable-data-reporting-common-esr.patch.

  third_party/rust/glean-core/src/lib.rs, third_party/rust/glean-core/src/core/mod.rs
      Glean upload/collection forced off inside glean-core (upstream 77f8fcd8,
      which replaced the old toolkit/components/glean/src/init/mod.rs hunk --
      on 157 build_configuration() uses a builder and that hunk rejects).
      glean-core is a vendored crate: scripts/librewolf-patches.py rewrites the
      two affected hashes in third_party/rust/glean-core/.cargo-checksum.json
      (upstream f072d15c). Those hashes are the 157 file hashes, which is why
      these hunks cannot be common: they apply to 153esr too, but there the
      checksum rewrite does not match and the vendored crate fails its check.
      The 153esr equivalent (init/mod.rs) is in
      patches/android/disable-data-reporting-common-esr.patch.

  (Gone: the browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabbrowser.js hunk that
  removed the UserInteraction "browser.tabs.opening" probes. Upstream dropped it
  in a1bd18fa for 156 and instead silences UserInteraction errors in
  toolkit/components/telemetry/core/Stopwatch.cpp, fb4c7a32 -- that part is
  in the common half.)

